agentsign.card.enrol.body:
Principal: {principal}
Label: {label}
Deckent generates the key on this host and keeps the private key in its own key store; it never leaves it (no backup, model, worker or log). With an active key and a policy grant this principal may sign catalog actions. A host signature proves this principal's enrolled key, through this host, at this time: attribution and a kill switch, not the model's intent.

agentsign.card.add.body:
Key: {keyId}
Purpose: {purpose}
Principal: {principal}
Label: {label}
External key: identity/attribution only, Deckent does not protect it. A key for skill import vouches for the skills it signed; it never acts by itself.

agentsign.card.revoke.body:
Key: {keyId} ({label}, {purpose})
Principal: {principal}
Every new, pending or replayed action with this key is refused from now on. The {count} committed rows it signed stay as they are and are shown as "signer revoked". The revocation is final; a new key needs a new enrolment.

agentsign.card.import.body:
Source: {source}
Pin: {pin}
Signed by key {keyId}
Imported only if the pin matches the received text and the signature verifies under an active import key of this scope at the moment it is saved.
